### Day 09 Lab — SCA Step-Up Authentication HTTP Exchange
### Replace all <PLACEHOLDER> values before sending requests.
### This file shows four phases: normal call, 401 trigger, step-up auth, payment retry.

### ============================================================
### PHASE 1: Normal API call — succeeds with initial single-factor token
### ============================================================

### 1a. GET account balance — succeeds (password-level ACR is sufficient for read)
GET https://<PLACEHOLDER-bank-api-host>/accounts/<PLACEHOLDER-account-id>/balances
Authorization: Bearer <PLACEHOLDER-initial-access-token>
Accept: application/json

### Expected response: 200 OK
### {
###   "account": {"iban": "<PLACEHOLDER-account-iban>"},
###   "balances": [{"balanceAmount": {"currency": "EUR", "amount": "5000.00"}, "balanceType": "closingBooked"}]
### }
###
### Token claims at this point:
###   acr: "urn:openid:params:acr:classes:password"   <- single-factor, password only
###   amr: ["password"]
###   scope: "accounts balances transactions"

---

### ============================================================
### PHASE 2: Payment attempt — triggers step-up 401
### ============================================================

### 2a. POST payment to new payee — high value, triggers SCA requirement
POST https://<PLACEHOLDER-bank-api-host>/payments/sepa-credit-transfers
Authorization: Bearer <PLACEHOLDER-initial-access-token>
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "instructedAmount": {
    "currency": "EUR",
    "amount": "1500.00"
  },
  "creditorAccount": {
    "iban": "<PLACEHOLDER-new-payee-iban>"
  },
  "creditorName": "<PLACEHOLDER-new-payee-name>",
  "debtorAccount": {
    "iban": "<PLACEHOLDER-debtor-iban>"
  },
  "remittanceInformationUnstructured": "Invoice payment"
}

### Expected response: 401 Unauthorized
### HTTP/1.1 401 Unauthorized
### WWW-Authenticate: Bearer error="insufficient_user_authentication",
###   error_description="SCA required: payment exceeds threshold and payee is not a trusted beneficiary",
###   acr_values="urn:openid:params:acr:mfa"
###
### Why this 401:
###   - amount=1500 exceeds TRA exemption threshold
###   - payee IBAN is not in the user's trusted beneficiary list
###   - current token acr=password is insufficient for MFA-required operation
###   - TRA engine evaluated: high risk, no applicable exemption
###
### The client must now initiate a step-up authorization flow.

---

### ============================================================
### PHASE 3: Step-up authorization — OIDC authorize + PAR
### ============================================================

### 3a. Push authorization request (PAR) to bind step-up parameters securely
POST https://<PLACEHOLDER-as-host>/as/par
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

response_type=code
&client_id=<PLACEHOLDER-client-id>
&redirect_uri=<PLACEHOLDER-redirect-uri>
&scope=openid+payments
&acr_values=urn%3Aopenid%3Aparams%3Aacr%3Amfa
&max_age=0
&prompt=login
&code_challenge=<PLACEHOLDER-pkce-code-challenge>
&code_challenge_method=S256
&authorization_details=%5B%7B%22type%22%3A%22payment_initiation%22%2C%22amount%22%3A%7B%22currency%22%3A%22EUR%22%2C%22amount%22%3A%221500.00%22%7D%2C%22creditorAccount%22%3A%7B%22iban%22%3A%22%3CPLACEHOLDER-new-payee-iban%3E%22%7D%7D%5D
&client_assertion_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Aclient-assertion-type%3Ajwt-bearer
&client_assertion=<PLACEHOLDER-signed-jwt-for-client-auth>

### Expected response: 201 Created
### {
###   "request_uri": "urn:ietf:params:oauth:request_uri:<PLACEHOLDER-request-uri-id>",
###   "expires_in": 90
### }
###
### Notes:
###   acr_values=urn:openid:params:acr:mfa    <- requires MFA-level authentication
###   max_age=0                                <- forces immediate re-authentication, ignores existing session
###   prompt=login                             <- explicit re-authentication required
###   authorization_details contains the specific payment (amount + payee) for dynamic linking
###   client_assertion_type and client_assertion are form body params (NOT Authorization: Bearer header)

---

### 3b. Redirect user to AS authorization endpoint with PAR request_uri
GET https://<PLACEHOLDER-as-host>/as/authorize
  ?client_id=<PLACEHOLDER-client-id>
  &request_uri=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Arequest_uri%3A<PLACEHOLDER-request-uri-id>

### AS presents SCA challenge to user:
###   Factor 1 (Possession): device-bound key in banking app authenticator
###   Factor 2 (Knowledge): PIN entered on device
###   Dynamic linking: AS generates authentication code from (device-key + amount=1500 + payee-IBAN)
###
### User approves on device → AS verifies dynamic link → issues authorization code

---

### ============================================================
### PHASE 4: Token exchange and payment retry
### ============================================================

### 4a. Exchange authorization code for step-up access token
POST https://<PLACEHOLDER-as-host>/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=authorization_code
&code=<PLACEHOLDER-authorization-code>
&redirect_uri=<PLACEHOLDER-redirect-uri>
&code_verifier=<PLACEHOLDER-pkce-code-verifier>
&client_id=<PLACEHOLDER-client-id>
&client_assertion_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Aclient-assertion-type%3Ajwt-bearer
&client_assertion=<PLACEHOLDER-signed-jwt-for-client-auth>

### Expected response: 200 OK
### {
###   "access_token": "<PLACEHOLDER-step-up-access-token>",
###   "token_type": "Bearer",
###   "expires_in": 300,
###   "scope": "openid payments"
### }
###
### Step-up access token claims (decoded):
###   {
###     "sub": "<PLACEHOLDER-user-id>",
###     "acr": "urn:openid:params:acr:mfa",          <- upgraded from password to mfa
###     "amr": ["mfa", "swk"],                        <- swk = software key (device-bound)
###     "authorization_details": [{
###       "type": "payment_initiation",
###       "amount": {"currency": "EUR", "amount": "1500.00"},
###       "creditorAccount": {"iban": "<PLACEHOLDER-new-payee-iban>"}
###     }],
###     "dynamic_link_verified": true,                <- dynamic linking was verified
###     "exp": <PLACEHOLDER-unix-timestamp>,
###     "jti": "<PLACEHOLDER-token-jti>"
###   }

---

### 4b. Retry payment with step-up access token — succeeds
POST https://<PLACEHOLDER-bank-api-host>/payments/sepa-credit-transfers
Authorization: Bearer <PLACEHOLDER-step-up-access-token>
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "instructedAmount": {
    "currency": "EUR",
    "amount": "1500.00"
  },
  "creditorAccount": {
    "iban": "<PLACEHOLDER-new-payee-iban>"
  },
  "creditorName": "<PLACEHOLDER-new-payee-name>",
  "debtorAccount": {
    "iban": "<PLACEHOLDER-debtor-iban>"
  },
  "remittanceInformationUnstructured": "Invoice payment"
}

### Expected response: 201 Created
### {
###   "paymentId": "<PLACEHOLDER-payment-uuid>",
###   "transactionStatus": "ACTC",
###   "debtorAccount": {"iban": "<PLACEHOLDER-debtor-iban>"},
###   "creditorAccount": {"iban": "<PLACEHOLDER-new-payee-iban>"},
###   "instructedAmount": {"currency": "EUR", "amount": "1500.00"}
### }
###
### What the RS verified:
###   1. Token signature is valid
###   2. acr=urn:openid:params:acr:mfa meets the requirement for this payment endpoint
###   3. authorization_details.amount matches the payment body amount (dynamic link check)
###   4. authorization_details.creditorAccount.iban matches the payment body payee (dynamic link check)
###   5. Token is not in the revocation list
###   6. Token is not expired
